# QCA6490 (WCN6855) Bluetooth NV/RF configuration table for liuqin.
#
# This is the vendor command sequence the stock Android BT HAL pushes to the
# controller at every Bluetooth enable; it is captured verbatim from the
# unit's own HCI traffic (btsnoop, 2026-10-06) and replayed by
# pkgs/bt-nv/default.nix.  All commands use OGF 0x3f (vendor).
#
# Without it the mainline stack left the BT RF section unconfigured: measured
# on the unit, the mouse (ATK Mouse BT) only linked when it was touching the
# tablet, while the same mouse worked 1 m away on stock Android with the same
# firmware, NVM, board file and rail voltages.
#
# One command per line, exactly the arguments of `hcitool cmd`.
0x3f 0x153
0x3f 0x157 ff
0x3f 0x017 14 01
0x3f 0x051 01 02 03
0x3f 0x051 10 4a 02 00 00 00 00 00 00
0x3f 0x051 0f 4a 02 00 00 00 00 00 00
0x3f 0x051 0b
0x3f 0x157 00 01
0x3f 0x157 06 00 04 8f 03 ff ff
0x3f 0x157 01 00 04 20 00 11 11 01 c4 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
0x3f 0x157 06 00 05 ff ff 4d ff ff ff
0x3f 0x157 01 00 05 20 00 11 11 01 c4 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
0x3f 0x157 07 00 06 95 fe 95 fe
